1. Error Correction Code (Hamming Code) – Viva Questions & Answers
What is Hamming Code?
Hamming Code is an error detection and correction technique used to detect and correct single-bit errors in data transmission.
Why are parity bits used?
Parity bits are used to check whether transmitted data contains errors.
How many parity bits are needed for 4-bit data?
3 parity bits are needed for 4-bit data.
What is the advantage of Hamming Code?
It can detect and correct single-bit errors automatically.
What is meant by encoded data?
Encoded data is the original data combined with parity bits.
What is error detection?
Finding whether transmitted data contains an error is called error detection.
What is error correction?
Identifying and fixing the error in received data is called error correction.
What happens in the receiver side?
Parity is checked again to detect the error position.
Which type of error is corrected here?
Single-bit error.
What is the output of the program?
It displays encoded data, received data, and detected error position.
