5. ARP / RARP Program – Viva Questions & Answers
What is ARP?
ARP (Address Resolution Protocol) converts IP addresses into MAC addresses.
What is RARP?
RARP (Reverse Address Resolution Protocol) converts MAC addresses into IP addresses.
What is a MAC address?
A unique hardware address assigned to a network device.
What is an IP address?
A logical address used to identify a device in a network.
Why is ARP required?
To communicate within a local network using MAC addresses.
What data structure is used in this program?
Dictionary.
What is an ARP table?
A table storing IP-to-MAC mappings.
What is the purpose of RARP?
To find the IP address from a known MAC address.
Is RARP commonly used today?
No, it is mostly replaced by DHCP and BOOTP.
What is the output of this experiment?
Mapped MAC or IP address is displayed.
