7. Distance Vector Program – Viva Questions & Answers
What is Distance Vector Routing?
A routing method where routers share routing information with neighbors.
Which algorithm is used in Distance Vector routing?
Bellman-Ford algorithm.
What is routing?
The process of selecting paths for data transmission.
What is a routing table?
A table containing route information to destinations.
What is cost in routing?
A value representing distance or path expense.
Why is minimum cost selected?
To find the shortest path.
What is neighbor information?
Routing information received from adjacent routers.
What is the advantage of Distance Vector routing?
Simple implementation.
What is the disadvantage?
Slow convergence and routing loops.
What is the output of the program?
Updated shortest path cost table.
